{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1566470301,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0ODM5MTE4NjI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3615","origin":"github"},"title":"Limit downloader jobs for `get` per target?","message":"AFAICS `datalad get` kicks of parallel downloaders by default. On a machine with lots of users that pull lots of files that can quickly grow into a number of connections that trigger firewall rules on the remote end that lead to seemingly broken network connections for any user on such a box.\n\nQ1: git-annex does serial by default and is no problem, we do parallel but go through a control master. Did anyone look into how this would look like from a server perspective? One connection, multiple serverside ssh-processes?\nQ 2: can we centrally reconfigure this behavior to go serial by default, in order to avoid having to instruct each user to use (and obey)  `get -J 1`, if that would be needed? I.o.w. can an admin somehow intervene without having to edit the sources?","files":null}]}